HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

PACE_VERSION added as traceability metadata; Kernel compatibility model clarified to depend only on SCHEMA_VERSION.

WHY

The President raised the update/compatibility model before it hardened
into the Contract by accident. Two distinct concerns were at risk of
being conflated: "which PACE engine version touched this instance"
(traceability) versus "which Contract shapes can this Kernel correctly
interpret" (compatibility). Also flagged: a Kernel should behave like a
browser reading HTML or Git reading old repositories — understanding a
range of dialects it knows, not treating every non-latest version as
"outdated" needing forced migration.

DECISION

Added PACE_VERSION (HAS_PACE_VERSION in the Ontology) to
contracts/INSTANCE_CONTRACT_0.1.0.pdl's ROOT_MANIFEST, explicitly
documented as traceability only, permanently — the Kernel never gates
what it can open on this field. Added services/version.py as the single
source of truth for PACE's own current engine version, consumed by
engines/project_creator.py when writing a new instance.

Confirmed, by reading the actual code rather than assuming, that the
Kernel already matched this principle before this session's changes:
validate_instance() only ever checks that PACE_VERSION is *present*
(via require_fields), never compares it against anything or uses it to
decide validity. The only compatibility gate is the SCHEMA_VERSION check
against SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS. Nothing needed correcting in that
regard — only the comments and the violation message did, since they
were written assuming "not supported" always means "the instance is
outdated," when a mismatch could equally mean the Kernel itself needs
updating (the same ambiguity a browser has with an unrecognized HTML
version). Reworded both to be neutral about which side is behind.

Added test_pace_version_mismatch_never_blocks_only_schema_version_does
to kernel/tests/test_kernel.py — constructs an instance with a
PACE_VERSION far from the current one but a supported SCHEMA_VERSION,
and asserts zero violations, proving the principle in code rather than
only in prose. Updated the existing fixture and the unsupported-version
test to include PACE_VERSION and to match the reworded message.

"Kernel Version" (the President's term in this discussion) and
PACE_VERSION are the same concept — no separate field was introduced for
it. "Instance Version" (a third concept proposed — the instance's own
version as its memory evolves, distinct from both PACE_VERSION and
SCHEMA_VERSION) was raised but not encoded: its trigger condition needs
sharper definition before it becomes a Contract field, and remains open.

All 17 tests (kernel 6, contract loader 4, project creator 4, CLI 3)
verified passing before this commit.

IMPACT

The Contract now states explicitly, not just by convention, that
compatibility is decided by SCHEMA_VERSION alone — the same principle a
future Migrator and a future multi-schema-version Kernel will both rely
on. PACE_VERSION carries history without ever becoming a second,
conflicting gate.

NEXT_STEPS

Define "Instance Version" precisely before adding it to the Contract.
Per the roadmap: adopt TuPeríMetro as the first governed project, then
implement pace create, then create Plataforma de Mantenimiento.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
